><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Contradicts the information on page 1, though I get that these are reports of "observations" and page 1 is more factual (?)</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="3" rect="583.885000,541.313000,768.353000,659.036000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260227111202-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260227111206-05'00'" name="3861398b-368e-44a5-8bad-871d159f1882" page="4" coords="56.693000,681.215000,160.066000,681.215000,56.693000,664.107000,160.066000,664.107000" rect="56.158400,663.572000,160.601000,681.750000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.6pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>there are references/summaries for 2024 and 2025 (and 2026!), but it's not explained anywhere why. This might be useful to orient readers.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="4" rect="408.727000,550.409000,592.654000,681.318000"
/></highlight
