><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>It's more complicated than that and linked to population abundance, distribution changes, and fishery viability</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="12" rect="408.872000,485.455000,592.799000,605.237000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260302064940-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260302070338-05'00'" name="6f52b270-2e88-4656-863d-b18166c27b19" page="12" coords="56.693000,557.252000,450.818000,557.252000,56.693000,543.135000,450.818000,543.135000" rect="56.251800,542.694000,451.259000,557.693000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>While technically true, this is a very incomplete description of the scallop situation in the Mid-Atlantic, where populations are suffering from multiple stressors.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
