><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>has exhibited slow growth since 2020, it </span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="25" rect="612.000000,295.555000,796.000000,387.555000"
/></caret
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223143337-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223143641-05'00'" name="47c3f298-f505-4c9f-8f94-e7b567b8a7e5" page="27" coords="449.494000,648.445000,555.305000,648.445000,449.494000,634.328000,555.305000,634.328000,56.693000,636.489000,516.841000,636.489000,56.693000,622.372000,516.841000,622.372000" rect="56.251800,621.931000,555.746000,648.886000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Emily Liljestrand"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>This seems like a very tricky thing to measure. Because you might see the same features in the data if a) the system is responding to changes without fundamentally changing composition or b) the system is not experiencing outside changes. If you see changes in composition and structure you know a system responded to changes without adaptive capacity. If you don't see changes in composition or structure, either it was adaptive or it didn't experience change. Will be interested to see how this is quantified in the next paragraphs...</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="27" rect="583.885000,464.583000,768.353000,648.525000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223144005-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223144019-05'00'" name="4326e06a-b4cd-4a9a-94f3-a95a9d7a1b6e" page="27" coords="454.074000,520.930000,555.311000,520.930000,454.074000,506.813000,555.311000,506.813000,56.693000,508.975000,478.345000,508.975000,56.693000,494.858000,478.345000,494.858000" rect="56.251800,494.417000,555.752000,521.371000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Emily Liljestrand"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>How are both things true? Changes in availability/abundance?</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="27" rect="583.885000,425.167000,768.353000,520.817000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223144608-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223144634-05'00'" name="f555c13e-c87d-4138-86df-b38ba8596aa8" page="27" coords="442.578000,317.692000,555.308000,317.692000,442.578000,303.575000,555.308000,303.575000,56.693000,305.737000,367.419000,305.737000,56.693000,291.620000,367.419000,291.620000" rect="56.251800,291.179000,555.749000,318.133000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Emily Liljestrand"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Consider changing to "other circumstances, like shark and large sport fish regulations and environmental conditions"</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="27" rect="583.885000,211.268000,768.353000,317.954000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223102901-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223102954-05'00'" name="34048b08-5c74-42f8-8af4-78b0ed4d5011" page="27" coords="99.967700,293.782000,555.307000,293.782000,99.967700,279.665000,555.307000,279.665000,56.693000,281.826000,149.051000,281.826000,56.693000,267.709000,149.051000,267.709000" rect="56.251800,267.268000,555.748000,294.223000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Robert Murphy"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I had commented about this in earlier drafts, but we need to be careful about inferring causality. fishing opportunities might have something to do with this but not all.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="27" rect="583.885000,165.020000,768.353000,293.779000"
/></highlight
><strikeout color="#F86464" creationdate="D:20260302072213-05'00'" flags="print" date="D:20260302072213-05'00'" name="e20cff98-e7d6-4a91-afc9-798fe2467248" page="29" coords="477.675000,452.650000,481.062000,452.650000,477.675000,438.533000,481.062000,438.533000" rect="473.465000,437.651000,485.272000,453.532000" subject="Cross-Out" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="29" rect="612.000000,360.650000,796.000000,452.650000"
/></strikeout
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223162518-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223162606-05'00'" name="9cfc0136-341d-4ede-b1a9-944b36db6fb3" page="29" coords="56.693000,512.495000,142.571000,512.495000,56.693000,498.239000,142.571000,498.239000" rect="56.247500,497.793000,143.017000,512.940000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Emily Liljestrand"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>For the ecological stability section, I'm surprised to not see a few fisheries species singled out and their biomass trends looked at. This could also fall under the previous section for fisheries though</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="29" rect="583.885000,383.648000,768.353000,512.408000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260223163550-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260223163652-05'00'" name="c9b37df6-dce2-4b7e-8a65-c4498128f4fc" page="29" coords="483.320000,464.605000,555.304000,464.605000,483.320000,450.488000,555.304000,450.488000,56.693000,452.650000,481.062000,452.650000,56.693000,438.533000,481.062000,438.533000" rect="56.251800,438.092000,555.745000,465.046000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Emily Liljestrand"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Extra space before the period. Also maybe this sentence can be cleaned up? Measures of the community show changes in the community? Could just say the shift is occurring, the measuring is implied</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="29" rect="583.885000,335.823000,768.353000,464.583000"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20260223163809-05'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" date="D:20260223163814-05'00'" name="35bb7316-84b3-419e-9df1-7959a6b0f0e0" icon="Comment" page="29" rect="89.956600,343.268000,113.957000,367.268000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Emily Liljestrand"
