><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>in-text references for Figures 39, 40?&#xD;&#xD;check throughout</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="592.144000,294.110000,776.071000,402.765000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260219090855-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260219090934-05'00'" name="5ee44fca-786c-4487-aefe-61e475314b5d" page="37" coords="204.118000,402.832000,244.389000,402.832000,204.118000,388.715000,244.389000,388.715000" rect="203.677000,388.274000,244.830000,403.273000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kiersten L Curti"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Figures should be included in the order they are cited, however, the citations jump from Figure 38 to 41</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="612.000000,310.832000,796.000000,402.832000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260219091104-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260219091115-05'00'" name="8a221a0d-d470-49ca-b587-123dee995df2" page="37" coords="264.137000,402.832000,452.502000,402.832000,264.137000,388.715000,452.502000,388.715000" rect="263.696000,388.274000,452.943000,403.273000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kiersten L Curti"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Need to add citations for Figures 39 and 40 here</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="499.199000,305.019000,682.908000,401.892000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260219092540-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260219092605-05'00'" name="1d43446b-2ca6-4cec-b591-e891348e04d1" page="37" coords="528.995000,402.832000,550.877000,402.832000,528.995000,388.715000,550.877000,388.715000" rect="528.554000,388.274000,551.318000,403.273000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kiersten L Curti"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I am not convinced this statement holds for spring and summer (Fig 39)</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="499.199000,217.310000,682.908000,310.692000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260219092619-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260219092639-05'00'" name="d2738d92-8c9c-468a-8f6e-daac8504c7d8" page="37" coords="76.371200,390.877000,108.199000,390.877000,76.371200,376.760000,108.199000,376.760000" rect="75.930000,376.319000,108.640000,391.318000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kiersten L Curti"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I am also not convinced this holds for the fall (Figure 40)</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="612.000000,298.877000,796.000000,390.877000"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20260309111959-04'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" date="D:20260309111959-04'00'" name="1336c8dc-c79e-4b0b-9cd5-69609bfe6df5" icon="Comment" page="37" rect="643.203000,568.581000,667.203000,592.581000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Joseph Caracappa"
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="37" rect="612.000000,500.581000,796.000000,592.581000"
/></text
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260305094959-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260305100917-05'00'" name="f9950858-9314-a840-bcdb-4994e7bbedb1" page="38" coords="322.350000,402.832000,555.310000,402.832000,322.350000,388.715000,555.310000,388.715000,56.693000,390.877000,555.310000,390.877000,56.693000,376.760000,555.310000,376.760000,56.693000,378.922000,555.305000,378.922000,56.693000,364.805000,555.305000,364.805000,56.693000,366.966000,555.309000,366.966000,56.693000,352.849000,555.309000,352.849000,56.693000,355.011000,372.466000,355.011000,56.693000,340.894000,372.466000,340.894000" rect="56.251800,340.453000,555.751000,403.273000" subject="Comment on Text" title="paula.fratantoni"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I suggest rewording this as below.  Since we are not showing a figure demonstrating the decreased stability of the GS, I suggest we remove that piece. 

"The Gulf Stream has been shifted north of its long-term mean position over much of the last decade (Figure 42).  However, since 2023 the Gulf Stream has shifted southward and remained close to its mean position. With this shift, the supply of Labrador Slope Water has increased along the Northwest Atlantic Shelf.  These changes are linked to the cooler water temperatures observed in 2024 and 2025 and shifts in the composition of source waters entering the Gulf of Maine through the Northeast Channel (see 2025 Highlights)"</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="38" rect="443.129000,69.378600,627.057000,359.998000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260305101438-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260305101518-05'00'" name="2c710d06-1e72-c14e-a876-de72462e411d" page="38" coords="56.693000,469.763000,555.304000,469.763000,56.693000,457.031000,555.304000,457.031000,56.693000,458.804000,121.297000,458.804000,56.693000,446.072000,121.297000,446.072000" rect="56.295100,445.674000,555.702000,470.161000" subject="Comment on Text" title="paula.fratantoni"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>are we no longer showing in situ observed bottom temperature time series as submitted each year?</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="38" rect="443.129000,360.653000,627.057000,469.962000"
/></highlight
