><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-17.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I'm quite cautious stating this with certainty for SNEMA yellowtail- this observation could be an artifact of the extremely low sample sizes in the recent time series or the truncated spatial area of survey catches moving northward. Maybe a change of wording here using "could have also shifted"</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="41" rect="612.129000,289.442000,796.055000,508.714000"
/></highlight
