/></caret
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260302074923-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260302074951-05'00'" name="f16d3be8-f903-4190-a1a6-b83bdd93a616" page="44" coords="533.722000,348.047000,555.309000,348.047000,533.722000,333.930000,555.309000,333.930000,56.693000,336.092000,414.383000,336.092000,56.693000,321.975000,414.383000,321.975000" rect="56.251800,321.534000,555.750000,348.488000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>consider moving this to after "environmental processes"</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="44" rect="592.144000,265.092000,776.071000,362.619000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260302075110-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260302075210-05'00'" name="529242fa-fe08-487e-9076-e6f9de37a75a" page="44" coords="367.320000,348.047000,530.912000,348.047000,367.320000,333.930000,530.912000,333.930000" rect="366.879000,333.489000,531.353000,348.488000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Not sure the wording here is as accurate as it could be. Perhaps "to guide phenological shifts"?</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="44" rect="592.144000,239.565000,776.071000,348.219000"
/></highlight
><strikeout color="#F86464" creationdate="D:20260302075505-05'00'" flags="print" inreplyto="d2d24584-9ba1-4cd6-bd6c-2f975e0f34af" IT="StrikeOutTextEdit" date="D:20260302075505-05'00'" name="1262a6e9-4962-4d75-ab2c-0e7ca6007d16" page="45" coords="169.089000,660.400000,201.221000,660.400000,169.089000,646.283000,201.221000,646.283000" replyType="group" rect="164.879000,645.401000,205.431000,661.282000" subject="Cross-Out" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="45" rect="612.000000,568.400000,796.000000,660.400000"
/></strikeout
><caret color="#F86464" creationdate="D:20260302075505-05'00'" flags="print" IT="Replace" date="D:20260302075535-05'00'" name="d2d24584-9ba1-4cd6-bd6c-2f975e0f34af" page="45" fringe="0.776489,0.776489,0.776489,0.776489" rect="195.503000,645.506000,206.938000,654.824000" subject="Inserted Text" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>effects on stocks are not well understood</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="45" rect="612.000000,562.047000,796.000000,654.047000"
/></caret
><strikeout color="#F86464" creationdate="D:20260302075736-05'00'" flags="print" date="D:20260302075736-05'00'" name="70a91f4b-39e3-431c-95d8-0ea5cb3dd998" page="45" coords="548.668000,443.221000,552.542000,443.221000,548.668000,429.104000,552.542000,429.104000" rect="544.458000,428.222000,556.752000,444.103000" subject="Cross-Out" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="45" rect="612.000000,351.221000,796.000000,443.221000"
/></strikeout
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260225094811-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260226152721-05'00'" name="14c6db2c-8a9e-4c31-b4fa-05afaaedef5d" page="45" coords="56.693000,684.310000,555.307000,684.310000,56.693000,670.193000,555.307000,670.193000,56.693000,672.355000,555.307000,672.355000,56.693000,658.238000,555.307000,658.238000,56.693000,660.400000,555.307000,660.400000,56.693000,646.283000,555.307000,646.283000,56.693000,648.445000,555.311000,648.445000,56.693000,634.328000,555.311000,634.328000,56.693000,636.489000,215.956000,636.489000,56.693000,622.372000,215.956000,622.372000" rect="56.251800,621.931000,555.752000,684.751000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Paul Nitschke"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I think this paragraph could be a little more specific on the risks to setting catch limits. I think the risks to setting catch limits are higher if we are relying on longer term projections (&gt; 3 years) along with the higher risk associated with the estimated Bmsy BRPs. Short term projections tend to better account for these effects through the inclusion of updated data inputs (changes in mean weights at age, selectivity, etc) and though updating the same associated effects on Fmsy regardless of whether these effects are environmentally driven or more due to fishing.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="45" rect="612.000000,592.310000,796.000000,684.310000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260224154629-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260227124839-05'00'" name="1d6d0b42-9d14-4f03-9a6d-59cf3701ea7a" page="46" coords="240.200000,124.569000,436.364000,124.569000,240.200000,111.837000,436.364000,111.837000" rect="239.802000,111.439000,436.762000,124.967000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Paul Nitschke"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>It is not completely clear to me how the  the small fish per large fish survey biomass anomaly were defined or developed. Were the length based conversions used for some of these stocks which could have an effect on the results? The bottom trawl survey does not produce reliable information for tilefish and probably should be remove since so few fish are caught in the survey.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="46" rect="612.000000,32.569000,796.000000,124.569000"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20260302080024-05'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" date="D:20260302080031-05'00'" name="961a145b-04fe-4bb2-a14f-3e4f4b69d1d7" icon="Comment" page="48" rect="287.999000,318.546000,311.999000,342.546000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>figure quality</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="48" rect="612.217000,250.546000,796.217000,342.546000"
/></text
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260224154026-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260227125114-05'00'" name="15f6f6bb-ffd0-40ff-aec1-136c15a638e4" page="48" coords="101.850000,708.677000,322.599000,708.677000,101.850000,694.560000,322.599000,694.560000" rect="101.409000,694.119000,323.040000,709.118000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Paul Nitschke"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>I think fish productivity and condition could also be potentially affected by overfishing. Perhaps, fishing effects is not meant to be part of this report but I think it can sometimes be difficult to disentangle fishing effects from environment effects.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="48" rect="612.000000,616.677000,796.000000,708.677000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260224161211-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260224163740-05'00'" name="0093ecf6-0720-4062-82be-36f678666e18" page="49" coords="385.602000,423.491000,477.783000,423.491000,385.602000,410.759000,477.783000,410.759000" rect="385.204000,410.361000,478.181000,423.889000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Paul Nitschke"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.4.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:10.5pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Wondering if it is a little miss-leading to plot the purple line on this plot? The trend seem to be driven by the first 6 data point in the the 1980s. There doesn't seem to be much of a trend after 1987 from eyeballing this.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="49" rect="612.000000,331.491000,796.000000,423.491000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#FF6200" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260302080431-05'00'" flags="print" date="D:20260302080431-05'00'" name="c8f41d41-6fd8-461b-b391-30cf22cefbe7" page="51" coords="266.349000,189.644000,291.995000,189.644000,266.349000,175.527000,291.995000,175.527000" rect="265.908000,175.086000,292.436000,190.085000" subject="Highlight" title="Kristan Blackhart"
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="51" rect="612.000000,97.643900,796.000000,189.644000"
/></highlight
><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20260227154902-05'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20260227155021-05'00'" name="d712677a-0eb7-455a-b3ab-bfe865bf6a55" page="51" coords="211.000000,305.385000,318.083000,305.385000,211.000000,292.653000,318.083000,292.653000" rect="210.602000,292.255000,318.481000,305.783000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Harvey Walsh"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Suggest adding that C. finmarchicus is the large taxon and C. typicus and Pseudocalanus spp. are the small taxa.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="51" rect="612.000000,213.385000,796.000000,305.385000"
/></highlight
